# Regenerable program output. CLAUDE.md states outright that tests/<set>/merged.png
# and tests/<set>/debug/ are safe to delete at any time. Together they are ~995 MB
# against the corpus's 73 MB of actual screenshots, so ignoring them is the
# difference between a ~100 MB repo and a 1.1 GB one.
#
# The *input* screenshots under tests/ are deliberately NOT ignored. They are the
# regression corpus: tools/baseline.py runs all 27 sets, and the ground-truth
# tables in CLAUDE.md key to those exact files. Note they carry player handles in
# the HUD -- badland_test3/cym.png reads "Waiting for yodagem..." across its top
# band -- which is why this repo is private. Redacting them is not the
# alternative: those pixels are documented program behavior (see the --top-crop
# residual note in CLAUDE.md's deferred section) and editing them would silently
# invalidate the baselines.
debug/
merged.png

# tools/baseline.py's stored run, captured on demand with -o. Regenerable, and a
# stale one sitting in the tree invites comparing against the wrong baseline.
before.json

# 194 MB, and rebuilds from requirements.txt, which is pinned.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The Discord token. polybot reads DISCORD_TOKEN from the environment and
# compose.yaml resolves ${DISCORD_TOKEN:?} from a .env beside it. Never commit it.
.env

# Editor and tool state, per-user rather than per-project. PyCharm keeps this
# project's per-test-set run configurations in .idea/workspace.xml, which
# JetBrains' own .idea/.gitignore already treats as local state.
.idea/
# vim leaves these beside the file being edited. Harmless except that one landed
# in `git add -A`'s list once, and a committed swap file is pure noise.
*.swp

# .claude/ wholesale, not just settings.local.json as this rule used to say.
# Claude Code keeps git worktrees under .claude/worktrees/, and each is a full
# second checkout carrying its own .git file. Because that .git is present git
# does not recurse into it: `git add -A` stages the directory as a single
# *gitlink* -- a submodule-shaped pointer to a commit that exists only in a
# local worktree, with no .gitmodules entry behind it. A repo in that state
# confuses status, clone and CI, and is fiddly to unpick afterwards.
.claude/

# Superseded, kept locally as a reference. Nothing imports it and the Dockerfile
# does not copy it.
polymerge_old.py

# Emoji artwork retired from the bot's flavor set, kept locally in case it is
# revisited. Safe to keep out of the repo: nothing reads Emojis/ at runtime --
# polybot names emoji by Discord snowflake (`<:wolfwait:1541528693430681660>`),
# so these PNGs are upload sources for the developer portal rather than assets --
# and the Dockerfile does not copy the directory either.
Emojis/unused/

# The predecessor bot's source, kept locally as a reference for how the merge
# used to work. Nothing imports it and the Dockerfile does not copy it, so this
# is the same call as polymerge_old.py above -- with one addition that makes it
# a hard rule rather than a tidy-minded one: it carries a live Discord bot token
# in committed source, so this directory must never be staged. (Not this bot's
# token, and it has never been in this repo's history -- keep it that way.)
#
# It is also 33 MB, nearly all of it duplicates: every render under its
# resources/overlays/ is byte-identical to the copy in Overlays/, which is where
# those files came from in the first place.
old mergebot-main/
